WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:08.122
After this video you can see what needs doing
in your organisation, invite new people,

00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:13.138
give stations to your teams, and ask members
to bring their own stations in.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.166
Your organisation has a page of its own.

00:00:17.286 --> 00:00:20.430
In the menu, click My organisation.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.010
This is your organisation's page.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.234
Its name is at the top, with a green label
saying Active.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:34.930
Four tabs sit below the name: Overview,
Stations, Members and Teams.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.578
The small number beside a tab says how many
there are.

00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:42.263
Overview starts with Needs your attention.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:47.999
It lists jobs waiting for you: stations nobody
can use yet, people in no team,

00:00:48.119 --> 00:00:50.927
and invitations nobody has answered.

00:00:51.047 --> 00:00:53.735
Each button takes you to the right place.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:01:01.822
Below are four counts: members, teams, stations, and
readings recorded in the last 30 days.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:04.822
Click the first three to open that tab.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.442
Teams shows each team with its people and its
stations.

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:12.610
General is everyone in the organisation.

00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:15.673
At the bottom is Your membership.

00:01:15.793 --> 00:01:19.513
Anyone can use Leave this organisation to step
out.

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:25.561
They keep their account and their own stations, but
lose the organisation's teams and stations.

00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:31.831
The Members tab lists everyone in your
organisation, with their role, their teams,

00:01:31.951 --> 00:01:34.039
and whether they are active.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:40.442
To find someone, type a name, username, email
or phone number in Search.

00:01:40.562 --> 00:01:42.698
The list shrinks to match.

00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:49.109
Each row shows the name, the username, and a
partly hidden phone number and email.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:52.541
Hiding part of them protects everyone's
privacy.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:59.758
The three dots at the end of a row open a menu:
Their stations, Add to a team, Change role,

00:01:59.878 --> 00:02:02.542
and Remove from organisation.

00:02:02.662 --> 00:02:05.278
Removing someone keeps their account.

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:09.491
This note counts people who are only in
General.

00:02:09.611 --> 00:02:12.515
Click Show them to list just those people.

00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.189
Tick two people.

00:02:15.309 --> 00:02:17.637
A bar appears above the list.

00:02:17.757 --> 00:02:20.805
Choose a team there, here Pump operators.

00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:23.489
Press Add to team.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.369
A green message says how many were added.

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:30.881
They join at once, because they are already in
your organisation.

00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:38.259
Below the list, Waiting to accept shows invitations
nobody has answered yet: the role, the team,

00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:40.971
when it was sent, and who sent it.

00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:45.791
Send again reminds the person, once an hour at
most.

00:02:45.911 --> 00:02:49.823
Withdraw takes the invitation back, after you
confirm.

00:02:49.943 --> 00:02:52.895
I keep this one, so I press Escape.

00:02:53.717 --> 00:02:56.981
To bring in someone new, press Add member.

00:02:57.101 --> 00:03:01.109
People are invited, and they join only when
they accept.

00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:05.805
Existing account is for someone who already
has OurWater.

00:03:05.925 --> 00:03:11.589
New managed account is for someone who cannot sign
up themselves: you make the account for them.

00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:16.473
Type the whole email address, username or
phone number.

00:03:16.593 --> 00:03:18.729
A part of it will not do.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.422
Choose their role.

00:03:21.542 --> 00:03:26.678
Data Contributor lets them record
measurements, and Viewer lets them only look.

00:03:26.798 --> 00:03:29.894
You can also pick a team for them to start in.

00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:32.589
Press Look up.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:38.181
OurWater shows only a name and a username, so
you can check it is the right person.

00:03:38.983 --> 00:03:41.839
If it is her, press Confirm invite.

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:46.663
Nothing changes for her yet, because she joins
only when she accepts.

00:03:47.483 --> 00:03:49.355
Press Done.

00:03:49.475 --> 00:03:55.451
She now appears under Waiting to accept,
newest first, with today's date and your name.

00:03:56.283 --> 00:04:01.227
The Stations tab lists the organisation's
stations and who can use each one.

00:04:01.347 --> 00:04:05.475
Nobody yet means only organisation admins can
use it.

00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:11.419
Search, Team, Type, Status and Country narrow
the list.

00:04:11.539 --> 00:04:16.051
Here I choose Rainfall under Type, and only
rain gauges stay.

00:04:16.883 --> 00:04:20.363
To give stations out, first choose who gets
them.

00:04:20.483 --> 00:04:25.451
Type a team or a person under Give access to,
then pick one from the list.

00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:28.299
Choose what they may do.

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:30.987
See shows the station on their map.

00:04:31.107 --> 00:04:33.603
Record lets them add measurements.

00:04:33.723 --> 00:04:37.299
Record plus edit lets them change its details
too.

00:04:38.117 --> 00:04:41.093
Tick the stations, then press Apply.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:46.901
Before anything changes, OurWater says how
many stations will change and who gets them.

00:04:47.717 --> 00:04:52.349
Confirm, and each station now names the team
and what it may do.

00:04:52.469 --> 00:04:57.101
To take access away, choose Take away and
apply the same way.

00:04:57.917 --> 00:05:02.213
Some stations belong to a member, not to the
organisation.

00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:05.981
Bring in stations lets you ask their owners to
bring them in.

00:05:06.101 --> 00:05:09.005
Nothing moves unless the owner agrees.

00:05:09.817 --> 00:05:13.513
Open the list, search for the station, and
tick it.

00:05:13.633 --> 00:05:16.081
Here it is Kavita's hand pump.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.803
Press Ask the owners.

00:05:18.923 --> 00:05:22.403
OurWater tells you how many requests will go
out.

00:05:22.523 --> 00:05:26.963
The owner gets a request, and nothing changes
unless they accept.

00:05:27.783 --> 00:05:29.823
The row now says Asked.

00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:36.063
Kavita will see the request on her Requests page,
and the station moves only if she accepts.

00:05:36.883 --> 00:05:41.995
The Teams tab lists each team with its leader,
its people and its stations.

00:05:42.115 --> 00:05:45.355
The two stations just given are counted here.

00:05:46.183 --> 00:05:50.359
To start another team, type a name here and
press Create.

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:54.055
Then open the team to add people and choose a
leader.

00:05:54.883 --> 00:05:58.195
Every organisation has a team called General.

00:05:58.315 --> 00:06:02.779
Everyone joins it automatically, so you never
add people to it.

00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:06.271
That is your organisation page.

00:06:06.391 --> 00:06:09.271
Overview shows what needs doing next.

00:06:09.391 --> 00:06:12.031
To look after one team, open it.

00:06:12.151 --> 00:06:16.999
To see how an owner answers a request, watch
the video on Requests.

00:06:17.817 --> 00:06:20.889
That is how to look after your organisation.

00:06:21.009 --> 00:06:23.673
Thanks for helping look after our water.
